A||||14||Standard||Fiero's, Fiero's everywhere!  and some racin'||||14||
Z||000000||Standard||07-14-2000||01:10 AM||||These last two days have been pretty good for Fiero sightings.. must be something about the Burnsville/Bloomington area in the morning.. Wedsnday morning I see a perfect looking dark green GT fastback, I zoom out after him but he takes a left into a parking lot and I'm too out of it to follow..  Then when I was headin' down 169 I saw a nice red 86/87 SE going the other way at a stop light.. as I pass I see a <B>very</B> cute woman at the wheel.. managed to grind going into 5th cause of that.. hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Today I managed to get behind a clean 87/88 coupe on 35w, stayed with him for awhile till I had to get on 62.  Also saw a very clean 85/86 coupe with some aftermarket wheels parked at Lake Harriet.  I need to print out some of those forum cards...<P>Also got to lay the smack down on some (un)worthy contenders.. heh.  First I pull up next to these 2 cuties in some mid/late 80's family hauler a few nights ago.. I didn't think they were gonna punch it, but they did.. needless to say they saw tail lights rather quickly.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Then when I was heading to Fleet Farm today there was some guy in a blue Escort Sport(woo hoo!) that was flooring it away from every stoplight.  I finally get up next to him at a light, and just blew him away.  <P>Man I love this car!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||My7Fieros||07-14-2000||03:18 AM||||It seems like I can go for weeks or months w/o seeing a Fiero..then one day I'll see several! Strange...usually I give the "thumbs up" and get one in return...other times I cant get the driver to look at me, thats when I'll get ahead of them to let 'em know they're not alone when it comes to Fieros...man I love these cars!!!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Jaei Sun||07-14-2000||03:59 AM||||Wow I usually see nice lookin' Fieros on 394... I was at the Minnetonka Audio King and there was a sweet lookin white GT Fastback that looked like it was leaking somthin. Other than that the only Fiero I see is one of my friends red w/sliver trim 86 GT... he keeps that car in showroom condition like all the time.  Right now it is getting the front end frame fixed cuz some woman hit em.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Standard||07-14-2000||03:38 PM||||Alright, another MN member!  Welcome to the forum!!  <P>I have yet to see any Fiero's on 394.. Your friend doesn't drive on 7 alot, does he?  When I worked at Bennett's cycle I would always see a sweet red GT driving down 7 around 5:30..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Raydar||07-14-2000||04:57 PM||||There's a guy (girl?) with a medium red Formula that occasionally takes a shortcut through the twisty roads that run past my neighborhood. Never have been in MY Formula when I saw the car, though. <I>Sure</I> couldn't keep up in the Sonoma (pig that it is).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
Z||000005||Uaana||07-14-2000||11:48 PM||||Well standard.. just in case you are wondering there are a couple of fieros one white (formula?) and another black coupe that look like they work at the ?printing place right across from fleet farm. and that beautiful red gt is still always parked out front of the "?pipe place" on 85th plus you can usually see my ragged out 87GT running around on 85th or at BP liquor on the weekends. (second job).||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jaei Sun||07-15-2000||03:24 AM||||He usually drives on 169, Right now he lives in the New Hope area right now but is moving pretty soon. He is driving his winter car right now, 84-85 silver coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phoenix||07-15-2000||02:24 PM||||I drive a red 88 coupe (with a GT nose and gold ground FX) east on 7 every day from St. Boni and catch 394 into Mpls. In the afternoon I'm back on 394 going west around 4:00 and then going west on 7. Seen several others over the past months - White 8? on 394, several red ones and a black one on 7 and one white Formula at checker autoparts at 7&101.<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000008||Standard||07-16-2000||01:35 AM||||Hmmm.. I'll have to keep my eyes open.  That black one on 7 mighta been me, Phoenix...<P>I finally got around to putting brake pads on the rear, and installed my braided brake lines to half of the car.. why half, you ask?  Because the #$*&%$ bleeder's are frozen into the calipers on the drivers side.. grrr  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  I'm gonna try to get those out Monday since I have a race in Mankato in about 9 1/2 hours...  <P>After I finished that work, I took a test cruise around Lake Calhoun and Harriet and boy was the rice out today.. heh.  I saw <B>the</B> worst purple/yellow paint scheme I have ever seen!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  Even though my car is kinda ratty I still got some looks..  I think we should all get together and cruise the lake someday, guys!  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
