Z||000011||Jaei Sun||07-16-2000||03:48 PM||||As far as I know there are 2 groups calling themselves MFF.  The first one wants money to join and to stay a member: "MFF dues are $20.00 per year, renewals due in January. New members accepted any time during year."<BR>The site is NEVER updated either: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org/</A> <P>The other seems to have like 6 members and is free like a car club should be I don't know how often this site is updated: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Downs/6120/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Downs/6120/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Uaana||07-16-2000||08:42 PM||||the MN board does update their site but just the events page. I paid the 20 buck for membership during their spring kick off. they really are a nice bunch of people. And as I understand it the dues are to help defray the cost of sending out news letters. member stickers and some of the event stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Phoenix||07-17-2000||12:08 AM||||I was driving up 169 today about 5:30pm and at the 694 turn off a maroon colored gt came up behind me with TALL wing risers. Belong to anyone of you guys?  I was in a red coupe with my daughter.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Standard||07-17-2000||02:23 AM||||Well I drove to Mankato and back today without seeing a single Fiero...  Did take the GT up above 100.. long flat empty stretch of highway and I just couldn't resist.. Put it in 4th and went, what a rush.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  Didn't keep it up there for long cause my bike was hanging off the back, though.  <P>I think I'm gonna see if I can make it to 1 of those club meeting's tonight, since I'll have nothing better to do..||||reg||1
